<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      The colour the launch window is painted in — the frame between the splash going and
      Compose drawing. It is the light scheme's `surface` (LightSurface in the design
      system's Color.kt) to the digit, with a `values-night` twin; a value that is merely
      close reads as a flash. Keep the two in step.
    -->
    <color name="launch_background">#FCFDFC</color>

    <!--
      The splash screen, and deliberately the one colour here with no night variant.

      The splash window is drawn by the system before this process exists, so it is
      resolved against the *system's* night mode — never against the theme the user chose
      inside the app. Painting it in the app's surface colour therefore only looks
      seamless while the two agree: pick Light on a phone set to dark and the splash comes
      up black and hands over to a white app. A brand colour is right in every
      combination, so the handover is a deliberate transition rather than a mismatch that
      shows up on some phones and not others.

      Pine30 from the palette: dark enough for the white mark to carry, and the middle of
      the gradient the launcher icon's background is drawn in.
    -->
    <color name="splash_background">#1C4B37</color>
</resources>
